Package: cixfan-dkms
Version: 1.1-2
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Roy Kaandorp <roykaandorp@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/royka1/cixfan
Depends: dkms (>= 2.1.0.0)
Recommends: linux-headers-edge-cix-p1 | linux-headers-generic | linux-headers
Description: quiet fan control for CIX Sky1 boards booted with ACPI
 On a CIX Sky1 board (Orange Pi 6 Plus / CIX Phecda) booted with ACPI rather
 than a devicetree, the firmware exposes only three fan profiles through the
 CIXHA024 ACPI device: automatic, mute and performance.  The automatic
 profile idles the fan at 40 % duty, which is considerably louder than the
 devicetree setup, where Linux drove the Chrome EC PWM itself from a pwm-fan
 cooling device.
 .
 This DKMS module restores numeric fan control without taking the I2C
 controller away from AML: it installs one small ACPI passthrough method over
 the firmware's own serialized \_SB.EC0.TRAS transport, puts the embedded
 controller into its undocumented manual fan profile, and then runs a quiet
 temperature curve driven from the SoC thermal zones.
 .
 It exposes a cix_fan_quiet hwmon device with pwm1 and pwm1_enable, and hands
 the fan back to the firmware's automatic profile on unload, reboot,
 shutdown, suspend, repeated EC errors or an emergency temperature.
